OL,3,GNEWSACare home told to improve low food
OL,4,Ahygiene score
OL,5,
OL,6,FA care home has been told "major
OL,7,Fimprovement" is needed to how it
OL,8,Fmanages food safety following an
OL,9,Finspection.
OL,11,FLonglands Care Home in Middlesbrough
OL,12,Fwas handed a food hygiene rating of one
OL,13,Fout of five, the second lowest score
OL,14,Fgiven by the Food Standards Agency.
OL,16,FIssues identified included how food is
OL,17,Fsafely managed and hygienic food
OL,18,Fhandling, while the cleanliness and
OL,19,Fcondition of facilities were deemed to
OL,20,Fbe generally satisfactory.
OL,23,APub: 12-NovQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB NE Eng NewsC Reg TVF Weather
